## Deploy

Deploy is via **Cloudflare Workers Builds** (CF dashboard → Workers & Pages →
Connect to Git → select this repo), not a GitHub Actions deploy job.

{%- if data_source == "postgres" %}
1. Create the real Hyperdrive config and replace the placeholder in
   `wrangler.jsonc`:
   ```
   pnpm dlx wrangler hyperdrive create {{ project_name }} --connection-string="<your production Postgres connection string>"
   ```
   Copy the returned `id` over `"REPLACE_WITH_HYPERDRIVE_ID"` in
   `wrangler.jsonc`, commit it — it's a config ID, not a secret. Deploying
   with the placeholder still in place would otherwise fail at query time,
   not at build time — `pnpm run predeploy` (below) catches it instead.
{%- endif %}
{{ "2" if data_source == "postgres" else "1" }}. Connect this repo in the Cloudflare dashboard.
{{ "3" if data_source == "postgres" else "2" }}. Set the deploy command to:
   ```
   pnpm run predeploy && pnpm dlx wrangler deploy --keep-vars
   ```
   `--keep-vars` is required — env vars/secrets below are set in the CF
   dashboard, and a plain deploy would wipe them on every push. `predeploy`
   fails the build if `wrangler.jsonc` still has an unfilled
   `REPLACE_WITH_*` placeholder.
{{ "4" if data_source == "postgres" else "3" }}. Set the vars/secrets listed below in the CF dashboard for this Worker.
{{ "5" if data_source == "postgres" else "4" }}. Route: `{{ project_name }}.propfirmmatch.solutions`.

