## Local development

```sh
cp .env.example .env
{%- if data_source == "postgres" %}
docker compose up -d      # local Postgres, matches DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING
{%- endif %}
pnpm install
{%- if data_source == "postgres" %}
pnpm db:generate && pnpm db:migrate   # first time only, or after schema.ts changes
{%- endif %}
pnpm dev
```
{%- if data_source == "postgres" %}

No migration ships with the template — `lib/db/schema.ts` starts with one
table (`examples`) precisely so `db:generate` has something to diff against
on a fresh clone. `drizzle/` is real app state (an append-only history
`drizzle-kit` owns), not template content, so it's created once here and
never touched again by `copier update`.
{%- endif %}

`pnpm dev` runs the frontend and the tRPC API (`server/router.ts`) together
in one process via `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` — no separate `wrangler dev`
needed.

**Windows:** `corepack enable pnpm` needs an elevated (Run as Administrator)
shell — it writes shims next to the Node install in `C:\Program Files\nodejs`,
which isn't user-writable otherwise. Without elevation, install pnpm the
same version `package.json`'s `packageManager` pins via
`npm i -g pnpm@<version>` instead, which needs no elevation. Also,
`winget install OpenJS.NodeJS` won't have the exact `.node-version` patch —
use `winget install OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS --version <version>`, or `fnm`/
`nvm-windows`, which read `.node-version` directly.
{%- if data_source == "postgres" %}

**No Docker?** `docker compose up -d` needs Docker Desktop, which on Windows
needs WSL2 or Hyper-V. A native Postgres (e.g. `winget install
PostgreSQL.PostgreSQL.17`) works fine, but two separate settings point at the
database and are read by different consumers — get both, or the dev server
stays aimed at the Docker-Compose default while migrations run somewhere
else:

| Setting | Read by |
|---|---|
| `hyperdrive[0].localConnectionString` in `wrangler.jsonc` | the dev server, via `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` |
| `DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING` in `.env` | `drizzle-kit` (`db:generate`/`db:migrate`) — runs as a Node CLI outside the Worker |
{%- endif %}

## Design system

`src/components/ui/`, `src/lib/utils.ts`, and `src/styles/globals.css` are
vendored from Prop Firm Match's shared Tailwind tokens + `packages/ui`
(trimmed). Local edits here may conflict on the next `copier update` —
that's expected; it's how brand-token updates propagate.

## Known gap

No error-tracking integration is included (PostHog was dropped from this
template's stack; no Sentry equivalent added). Accepted for now.
